# tools/crypto_signed_carry_witness.rish — the signed carry, Season G's FIRST composition over the GREEN Monocypher-parity primitives: a
# self-describing, content-addressed, Ed25519-signed carry frame built purely from BLAKE2b-512 (the content address) and Ed25519 sign/verify
# (the seal), authoring no new cryptography (Season G · Cryptography).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G names the signed carry as the
# Lotus "who made this record" unblock, and Season 2 Journey 6's content-addressed chain of custody).
# Kin: crypto/blake2b.rye · crypto/ed25519_sign.rye · crypto/ed25519_verify.rye (the GREEN primitives this composes) ·
# crypto/sealed_session.rye (the confidentiality twin). Monocypher (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual) is the parity TARGET of the primitives
# beneath, never a copied line — our own composition, studied clean-room (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# crypto/signed_carry.rye builds a carry frame magic GSC1 ‖ signer pubkey ‖ paylen (u64 big-endian) ‖ payload ‖ BLAKE2b-512 digest ‖
# Ed25519 signature-over-digest, authoring no new cryptography: it composes the GREEN BLAKE2b-512 (the content address) and the GREEN
# Ed25519 sign/verify (the seal). Signing the digest makes it do double duty as both the content address a keeper cites and the value the
# signature commits to. open() verifies BEFORE trust: magic, then declared length, then a recomputed digest (a byte moved anywhere upstream
# is refused here, before the signature is consulted), then the signature — only then does one zero-copy payload byte leave the door,
# alongside the verified signer key. Parity holds at selftest against an independent BLAKE2b digest and the primitive verify path.
# Purely local over a TEST seed — no real identity key, no network, no funds, no real device; sealing a record with the maintainer's own
# identity key stays the custody gate, and constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_signed_carry_witness.rish

say "crypto-signed-carry: Language EN — Season G's FIRST composition over the GREEN Monocypher-parity primitives: the fourteen rungs before it authored the primitives, and this one composes two of them into the shape every module that records provenance reaches for. crypto/signed_carry.rye builds a self-describing, content-addressed, Ed25519-signed carry frame purely from BLAKE2b-512 (the content address) and Ed25519 sign/verify (the seal), authoring no new cryptography of its own. This is the decision wave's Lotus 'who made this record' unblock and Season 2 Journey 6's content-addressed chain of custody, standing as a library on primitives already parity-GREEN."
say "crypto-signed-carry: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a frame is magic GSC1, signer pubkey, paylen (u64 big-endian), payload, BLAKE2b-512 digest, and an Ed25519 signature over that digest — signing the digest makes it do double duty as both the content address a keeper cites and the value the signature commits to, so one seal answers both 'is this the same bytes' and 'who signed them.' open verifies before trust — magic, then declared length, then a recomputed digest, then the signature — and only then does one zero-copy payload byte leave the door, alongside the verified signer key."
say "crypto-signed-carry: Lens TAME — the composition authors no new cryptography; it turns two proven stones into one usable seal, bounds the payload at a named ceiling, and asserts its contracts on every function. GREEN on the first metal pass: round-trip across eight payload lengths (empty through 64 KiB), byte-identical determinism, an independent BLAKE2b plus primitive-verify cross-check, and seven refusals each caught by its OWN named error — a tampered payload, a spliced digest, and a swapped signer all fail DigestMismatch, a flipped signature byte fails BadSignature (proving the paths are distinct), plus bad magic, two truncations, and an undersized buffer. Purely local over a TEST seed — no real identity key, no network, no funds, no device; sealing a record with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate, and constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/signed_carry"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/signed_carry.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-signed-carry: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/signed_carry.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-signed-carry: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-signed-carry: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-signed-carry' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-signed-carry: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-signed-carry line"
